Hello 1.0 for RISC OS
=====================

An example program from riscos-crossdev: a small C program cross-compiled
on Linux with GCCSDK GCC 10.2, checked, and zipped with RISC OS filetypes.

Double-click !Hello. A task window opens and shows:

  Hello, world! This machine has been up for H:MM:SS.
  checksum 1653a4a4

To be greeted by name, type *Set Hello$Name <your name> first.

Requirements: RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine with VFP (a Raspberry Pi 2
or later, or a Cortex-A8/A9 board); SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later and
ARMEABISupport, both from PackMan.

